.TH ORAN-DHCP-GEN 1 "@DATE@" "@VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oran-dhcp-gen \- O-RAN DHCP configuration generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oran-dhcp-gen
\fIoran_dhcp.yaml\fR
[\fB\-\-target\fR \fI{isc,kea,all}\fR]
[\fB\-\-outdir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-deploy\fR]
[\fB\-\-restart\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates DHCP server configuration files from a YAML data model.
When used with --deploy, backs up existing config files with a
timestamped suffix before overwriting them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-target {isc,kea,all}
Output target (default: isc).
.TP
.B \-\-outdir DIR
Output directory (default: temp dir when --deploy, current dir otherwise).
.TP
.B \-\-deploy
Deploy generated configs to system paths with timestamped backups.
Requires root/sudo to write to /etc/dhcp/, /etc/kea/, /etc/default/.
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Restart DHCP services after successful deploy. Requires --deploy.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH "YAML SCHEMA (v2.2.0)"
The YAML model has four top-level sections plus oru_classes:
.TP
.B global
default_lease_time, max_lease_time, oran_enterprise_id (53148).
.TP
.B controllers
List of named controllers with ipv4 and ipv6 addresses.
.TP
.B lease_profiles (optional, NEW in 2.2.0)
Named reusable lease parameter sets. Reference from a class via
\fIlease_profile: <name>\fR. Generator emits these at POOL scope
(where they take effect in ISC) and as per-class lifetimes in Kea.
.TP
.B ca_ra_profiles (optional, NEW in 2.2.0)
Named reusable TLS CA/RA bootstrap settings (CA server IP, URI path,
subject DN, app protocol, NETCONF mode byte). Reference from a class
via \fIca_ra: { profile: <name>, port: N, ... }\fR.
.TP
.B oru_classes
List of O-RU classes. \fIipv4_range\fR and \fIipv6_range\fR are now
both optional (NEW in 2.2.0); omit to disable that family for the class.
At least one must be present.
.SH DEPLOY PATHS
.TP
dhcpd.conf \-> /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.conf
.TP
dhcpd6.conf \-> /etc/dhcp/dhcpd6.conf
.TP
isc-dhcp-server \-> /etc/default/isc-dhcp-server
.TP
kea-dhcp4.conf \-> /etc/kea/kea-dhcp4.conf
.TP
kea-dhcp6.conf \-> /etc/kea/kea-dhcp6.conf
.SH BACKUP FORMAT
Backups are named: <original_file>.bak.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS
Example: /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.conf.bak.20260504-143022
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate ISC DHCP configs to current directory:
.B oran-dhcp-gen oran_dhcp.yaml
.TP
Generate and deploy ISC DHCP configs with backup:
.B sudo oran-dhcp-gen oran_dhcp.yaml --deploy
.TP
Generate, deploy, and restart ISC DHCP:
.B sudo oran-dhcp-gen oran_dhcp.yaml --deploy --restart
.TP
Full Kea DHCP workflow:
.B sudo oran-dhcp-gen oran_dhcp.yaml --target kea --deploy --restart
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR kea-dhcp4 (8),
.BR kea-dhcp6 (8),
.BR dhcp-lease-list (1)
